    "PROOF": {
      "L0_DEGREE": "22*3 + 27*2 = 120 = 20*6 and 22 + 27 = 49, so every number of 1..49 has frequency exactly 2 or 3. Overlap <= 1 means distinct numbers of a ticket v reach disjoint neighbour sets, so deg(v) = sum_{x in v}(f(x)-1) = 2t(v) + (6-t(v)) = 6 + t(v). Profile 5^12 1^6 0^2 gives degrees 11^12, 7^6, 6^2 and |E| = 93 = 3*22 + 27.",
      "P1_S1_WEDGES": "W = sum C(deg,2) = 12*55 + 6*21 + 2*15 = 816. T counts all triangles of G; each closes exactly 3 wedges and each closed wedge lies in exactly one triangle, so O = W - 3T = 816 - 810 = 6.",
      "P1_S2_EDGE_IDENTITY": "For an edge uv the open wedges with arm uv are: centre u, other end w in N(u)-{v}, w not in N(v), numbering (deg u - 1) - |N(u)&N(v)| because N(u)&N(v) is a subset of N(u)-{v}; symmetrically for centre v. An open wedge has exactly two arms, so sum_{uv in E}[deg u + deg v - 2 - 2|N(u)&N(v)|] = 2O = 12 with every summand >= 0.",
      "P1_S3_HL_BOUND": "H = the 12 degree-11 tickets, L = the other 8, c = e(H,L). For an edge uv, u in H, v in L: N(u)&N(v) is a subset of N(v)-{u}, so |N(u)&N(v)| <= deg v - 1 <= 6 and the u-side term is >= 10 - 6 = 4; the v-side term is >= 0. Dropping the other (nonnegative) summands: 4c <= 12, so c <= 3.",
      "P1_S4_PARITY": "sum_{u in H} deg u = 132 = 2e(H) + c, so c is even: c in {0, 2}.",
      "P1_S5_C_EQUALS_2_EXCLUDED": "c = 2 gives e(H) = 65 = C(12,2) - 1: exactly one pair x,y in H is non-adjacent and each of the other 10 H tickets is adjacent to both, giving 10 distinct open wedges x-z-y. O >= 10 > 6, a contradiction.",
      "P1_S6_RESULT": "c = 0: e(H) = 66, G[H] = K12; G[L] has degree sum 54, e(L) = 27 = C(8,2) - 1, so G[L] = K8 - e where e joins the two degree-6 tickets (the only L vertices below 7). Consistency: T = 220 + (56 - 6) = 270, O = 0 + 6 = 6. G = K12 disjoint-union (K8 - e).",
      "P2_S1_LABEL_SIDES": "Tickets sharing a number are adjacent and c = 0, so every label lies wholly in H or in L. An H ticket (t = 5) carries 5 triple labels and 1 pair label, all inside H: 12*5/3 = 20 triple supports and 12/2 = 6 pair supports. L carries 6*1/3 = 2 triple and (6*5 + 2*6)/2 = 21 pair labels (totals 22 and 27).",
      "P2_S2_MATCHING": "Each H ticket lies in exactly one H pair label, so the 6 pair labels partition the 12 H tickets: a perfect matching.",
      "P2_S3_STS13": "G[H] = K12 with overlap <= 1, so any two H tickets share exactly one label: a linear space on the 12 H tickets with 20 lines of size 3 and 6 of size 2. Adding a new point inf to the 6 pair lines covers every pair of the 13 points exactly once with 26 triples: an STS(13) S with distinguished point inf. Conversely the H part (tickets, labels, incidences) is recovered from (S, inf) by deleting inf. H tickets use only H labels (5 + 1 = 6 numbers).",
      "P2_S4_L_UNIQUE": "The 2 L triple labels contain only t >= 1 tickets, i.e. the six degree-7 tickets, each exactly once: two disjoint triples A, B partitioning them; the degree-6 tickets a, b carry none. Every edge of G[L] is realized by exactly one label; A and B take the 6 triangle edges, so the 21 pair labels are exactly the remaining 27 - 6 = 21 edges of K8 - ab. The L incidence structure is determined by (A, B, {a, b}) and any two choices are related by a ticket bijection: unique up to isomorphism (generator FIXED_EIGHT_TICKETS).",
      "P2_S5_INVARIANCE": "OFFICIAL_ANY_PRIZE wins on (D, s), s not in D, iff some ticket t has |t&D| >= 3, or |t&D| = 2 and s in t. For sigma in Sym(1..49), (D, s) -> (sigma D, sigma s) is a bijection of the outcome space with |sigma t & sigma D| = |t&D| and sigma s in sigma t iff s in t, so count(sigma P) = count(P). Success is a union over tickets, so ticket order and relabelling are irrelevant. Portfolio SHA is not invariant and is not used as an identity.",
      "P2_S6_COVERAGE": "All 49 numbers are used, each in >= 2 tickets, and distinct numbers have distinct ticket sets (overlap <= 1); so a realization P is determined up to Sym(49) by its ticket-label incidence structure, which is (H part) + (L part) on disjoint labels. By P2_S3-S4 its isomorphism type is fixed by the pointed STS(13) (S, inf). By the classification S is isomorphic via some phi to a generator representative R_i (CYCLIC or NONCYCLIC), hence (S, inf) ~ (R_i, q) with q = phi(inf), and the generator candidate (R_i, q) has pointed STS isomorphic to (R_i, q). Therefore P = sigma(C) for a ticket bijection and sigma in Sym(49) with C a family member, and count(P) = count(C). The family takes all 13 deletion points of both representatives, so it covers every isomorphism type of the cell (in fact one per Aut(R_i)-orbit).",
      "P3_ACCOUNTING": "Each family member carries an explicit verified (ticket map, number map) certificate onto its class recount target; each class target is freshly recounted with the pinned canonical evaluator, so every realization's exact count equals one recounted class count, and the cell maximum is the maximum over classes."
    },
